    description: "Spec §9.901 documents the usage_context id form as 'id': 'uc:...'; the substrate (and a fresh run) emit 'usage:sha256:...'. 0/8 usage_contexts use the documented prefix. Substrate: all 8 usage_contexts ids have prefix 'usage' (e.g. usage:sha256:20d859135eb74337). Spec docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:909 example: 'id': 'uc:...'; §923 'id: Unique identifier'. Fresh hypergumbo run on packages/hypergumbo-tracker reproduces: id usage:sha256:20d859135eb74337. Scope: all usage_context records (8/8 in this corpus). Consequence: a consumer matching the documented uc: id prefix to filter/join usage_contexts gets 0 matches. Cosmetic-ish but the spec marks this surface 🟩 done."  # 050c
    fields: {}  # 050c
- op: discuss  # ce8c
  at: '2026-06-06T04:15:13Z'  # ce8c
  by: agent  # ce8c
