- op: discuss  # a85e
  at: '2026-07-30T16:48:47Z'  # a85e
  by: agent  # a85e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a85e
  clock: 4  # a85e
  nonce: a85e  # a85e
  message: "DONE — the SPEC was wrong, and it was the only artifact carrying the wrong value.\n\nMeasured: all 20 usage_contexts on a fresh self-survey use the 'usage:' prefix (sample: usage:sha256:8b88608c3173ab8b), emitted by ir.py:1080. The spec's example showed 'uc:...'. A consumer implementing the documented filter matched 0 of 20, which is the filed consequence.\n\nFixed the SPEC, not the emitted value, and the reasoning is worth keeping because the opposite call would also have been defensible. Grepping the whole tree for 'uc:' found exactly ONE occurrence — the spec example itself. No code, no test, no schema, no fixture expects it. So the emitted value is not merely dominant, it is unopposed, and changing it would churn a serialized identity value to adopt a prefix nothing uses.\n\nIt would also have inverted WI-talos Ruling 4, which explicitly REJECTED the mechanical contraction of identity prefixes (hgsid9:/hgshid4:) on the grounds that readable prefixes are the point. 'uc:' is the terse form of 'usage:'; adopting it would be that own-goal in miniature. Same 'reconcile the letter to the verified reality' move as the META-jotih statement amendment (register pt.19)."  # a85e
